# Give access to the dma-buf heaps.
#
# devtmpfs creates /dev/dma_heap/* with mode 0600 and owner root:root, and
# nothing in the base system relaxes that. libcamera opens the system heap
# for its software ISP: without it the ISP cannot allocate its buffers and
# debayering is disabled, which leaves the camera with no usable stream and
# hides it from camera applications.
#
# The nodes are opened by the session daemons, not only by the applications.
# WirePlumber starts early in the boot and enumerates libcamera before the
# seat ACL exists, which used to leave the ISP disabled until the session
# manager was restarted by hand.  A world readable node removes that race:
# a dma-buf heap is a plain anonymous allocator, so letting every local user
# open it grants nothing beyond what they can already allocate from the
# kernel themselves.
SUBSYSTEM=="dma_heap", MODE="0666"
